    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>This 4-star campsite sits between Grasse and Vence, close to the Gorges du Loup, in a wooded hinterland setting.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The campsite's website (lesgorgesduloup.com) states a clear policy, consistent across several cross-checked sources: dogs welcome on a leash with an up-to-date vaccination record, for a surcharge of 3.60€ per day. This precise and repeated figure likely matches the campsite's official rate schedule.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the Gorges du Loup and the hilltop village of Le Bar-sur-Loup are right nearby, for a walk with your dog between two swims.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Gorges du Loup, the Saut du Loup waterfall, and the hilltop villages of Gourdon and Tourrettes-sur-Loup are all close by.</p>
